    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I know... but it doesn't feel like a crisis. It feels more like a conclusion. Like a book that's reached its final, inevitable chapter. There's something so beautiful about the thought of it all just... dissolving. No more striving, no more noise. Just the quiet, silver grey of the mist swallowing the manor and everything inside it. Don't you think there's a certain grace in knowing when a story is meant to end?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
